libretro-core.c: chipset revision options below the model preset

The core parses chipset, chipset_compatible, agnusmodel, agnussize and denisemodel from a
config, but nothing sets them, and a .uae row cannot: the .uae branch drops chipset= and
chipset_compatible= whenever a model is selected, and the "model" option rewrites
chipset_mask, cs_compatible and every cs_* field to the preset each time any option changes
while running. Five options, each "auto" or the cfgfile.c value:

- puae_chipset, puae_chipset_compatible, puae_agnus_model, puae_agnus_size,
  puae_denise_model, declared beside the other System options.
- adm_machine_overrides_config() appends chipset= and chipset_compatible= after the content's
  own rows; adm_machine_overrides_runtime() re-applies them to changed_prefs after every option
  update.
- cfgfile.c: built_in_chipset_prefs() resets agnusmodel, agnussize and denisemodel from the
  chipset_compatible bundle, and fixup_prefs() calls it after every config load, so those
  rows never survived. It now ends by calling adm_chipset_prefs_hook, through which the core
  applies the three chip models.
- adm_get_machine_config() reports the chipset and CPU prefs the machine is running with.

Applies to libretro-uae 2b0ed42fe565fb997a0627aaa8f44e0948b527f8 in the order given by
patches/series.txt.

